/**
 * Grade 9 informational articles: 50 of them, five for each of RI.9-10.1 to
 * RI.9-10.10, alternating science and social studies.
 *
 * Held to the bands in scripts/reading-article-plan.json: seven or eight
 * paragraphs, a higher version at LL 1140-1260 and a lower one at LL
 * 920-1020 with the same lettered paragraphs, five questions of the five
 * named kinds. These are written at eight throughout.
 *
 * Two things change at grade 9. The standards are shared with grade 10, so
 * the same ten are met twice at different depths, and RI.9-10.9 names
 * actual documents: Washington's Farewell Address, the Gettysburg Address,
 * the Four Freedoms, King's Letter from Birmingham Jail. That standard is
 * about particular American texts and how they answer each other, so its
 * five articles are all social studies rather than alternating, which is
 * the one place this grade departs from the house pattern and does so
 * because the standard requires it.
 *
 * RI.9-10.8 adds identifying false statements and fallacious reasoning,
 * which is a harder job than judging sufficiency: a reader has to name the
 * move, not only distrust the conclusion. Its five articles each contain
 * one named fallacy doing real work in an argument somebody actually makes.
 *
 *   bun run scripts/articles/g9.src.mjs && bun run scripts/merge-articles.mjs
 *   bun run scripts/check-articles.mjs
 */
