      "It also has the worst possible vantage point. A person is explaining their own life to themselves as well as to a reader, the account was composed after everything had already turned out, and memory reorganises around outcomes.",
      "A biography trades access for distance. The writer cannot know what the subject intended and can read letters the subject forgot writing, interview people who disliked them, and compare claims against dates.",
