      "Its completeness is what makes it the reference. Any claim about what was said can be checked against it, and the parts that are boring are not omitted, which is precisely why it can settle a dispute.",
      "A courtroom sketch records something the transcript cannot. It shows where people sat, how they held themselves and who was looking at whom, and in courts that exclude cameras it is the only visual record there is.",
      "It is also an interpretation made at speed. An artist chooses a moment, chooses who to put in the frame and chooses what expression to give them, and a face drawn as composed or as anguished is a judgement.",
      "A documentary or podcast adds narrative and removes nearly everything. A trial of six weeks becomes eight hours, which means more than ninety-five per cent of it is gone, and what remains was chosen for being interesting.",
